> f(x: real) = sin(x)^2 + cos(x)^2
> g(x: real) = 1
> equiv f g
f and g are equal on the domain of f (proved by algebra: f - g simplifies to 0 over Q)
> h(x: real) = sin(x)^2
> k(x: real) = 1 - cos(x)^2
> equiv h k
h and k are equal on the domain of h (proved by algebra: f - g simplifies to 0 over Q)
